      <div class="th-keybox">
        <b>The whole lecture in one line.</b> Nothing can feel temperature. So every thermometer picks a property that changes with heat, fixes two known points, and works out everything in between as a straight-line proportion - which turns the gas, resistance, mercury and faulty-thermometer formulas into one single formula.
